The rule `re-lint/prefer-early-return`: "The happy path is wrapped in this if while 2 statement(s) dangle after it — flip to `if (!(…))` guarding the tail and let the happy path run flat."

So at 141:9 (`if` at column 9 — `        if (round === 2) {`), the if-block ends with `return;` and then 2 statements dangle after it (lines 151, 152: `yield {type:'text'...}` and `yield {stop...}`). The rule wants the pattern flipped: instead of `if (cond) { happy-path; return; } tail;`, do `if (!cond) { return .../yield...; } happy-path flat;`.

